 ## Overview
-This method computes the radiative transfer equation for participating media by splitting it into incremental terms for $K$ scattering orders, allowing precomputation of multiple scattering effects that would otherwise require exponentially complex recursive Monte-Carlo evaluation [S1]. It differs from [Bounced Multiple Scattering](3532-bounced-multiple-scattering.md) by using explicit integral precomputation of auxiliary fields rather than ray-bouncing, and from [GPU Implementation of Precomputed Multiple Scattering](4706-gpu-implementation-of-precomputed-multiple-scattering.md) by focusing on the mathematical formulation and data layout rather than hardware-specific optimization.
+This method computes the radiative transfer equation for participating media by splitting it into incremental terms for $K$ scattering orders, allowing precomputation of multiple scattering effects that would otherwise require exponentially complex recursive Monte-Carlo evaluation [S1]. It builds on [Precomputed Multiple Scattering Table](3324-precomputed-multiple-scattering-table.md) and differs from [Bounced Multiple Scattering](3532-bounced-multiple-scattering.md) and [GPU Implementation of Precomputed Multiple Scattering](4706-gpu-implementation-of-precomputed-multiple-scattering.md) by relying on explicit integral precomputation of auxiliary fields rather than ray-bouncing or hardware-specific optimization [G].
 
